  "conclusion": "The upstream wait removal changes the failure from a stall to a software reset loop. The diagnostic unpatched source rebuild has an ES8388 initialization assertion under the subsequent panic/stalled-state sequence. No ordinary lane produced a complete frame. The upstream workaround does not reach application readiness: the same assertion is still executed in the patched source build. Adding generic codec-address register files in the approved native backend did not yield a complete frame or valid transmitted-audio capture from the published BIN.",
  "limits": "Native isolated Device Service only. No audio, ready UI, touch, hardware or browser verification in these runs. The official BIN lacked a matching ELF and was not replaced; source-built artifacts have different hashes from the published BIN. The two generic codec-address register files do not implement audio codec semantics; this run tested only a controller routing hypothesis.",
  "burner": "NOT SUBMITTED"
}
